{
  group post-grant-group
  note "A third party (or, for reexam, anyone including the owner) attacks the issued patent. Three doors, decided by the CHALLENGER: inter partes review (IPR, 102/103 on patents/publications, subject to the 315(b) one-year bar), post-grant review (PGR, broad grounds incl. 101/112 but only within 9 months of grant), or ex parte reexamination (EPR, SNQ standard, no petitioner estoppel). This is the first genuinely ADVERSARIAL region of the chart — the outcomes are opposing-party draws, not examiner draws."
