state ipr-petition-filed: "IPR Petition Filed" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 311–314; 37 CFR 42.107"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Petitioner filed an IPR petition. The patent owner may file a Patent Owner Preliminary Response (POPR) within 3 months — arguing discretionary denial (Fintiv/325(d)) and/or the merits — or waive it and reserve arguments for trial. Then the Board decides institution."
  ipr-popr-filed "File Patent Owner Preliminary Response (POPR)" -> ipr-institution-decision {
    authority cite "37 CFR 42.107; 35 U.S.C. 313"
    effort 60.hours
    within ipr-preliminary-response {
      extendable false
      note "POPR due within 3 months of the notice according the petition a filing date. Optional; argue discretionary denial and/or the merits."
    }
    duration { min 13.5.days, mode 45.days, max 90.days }
  }
  ipr-popr-waived "Waive POPR — reserve arguments for trial" -> ipr-institution-decision {
    authority cite "37 CFR 42.107(b)"
    effort 0.5.hours
  }
}

chance ipr-institution-decision: "IPR Institution Decision" by office discretion effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 314(a); 37 CFR 42.108"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "The Board institutes only on a reasonable likelihood the petitioner prevails on ≥1 claim (35 U.S.C. 314(a)); it may deny on discretionary grounds. Institution rate authored at 0.65 — APPROXIMATE, a mid-2010s–2020s historical order of magnitude (institution rates have varied ~0.55–0.68 across vintages/PTAB policy); flagged, not a live figure."
  court_listener_url "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/3214886/cuozzo-speed-technologies-llc-v-lee/"
  edge-ipr-institution-decision-ipr-trial-instituted "PTAB institutes trial (35 U.S.C. 314(a))" -> ipr-trial-instituted p 0.65 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 314(a); 37 CFR 42.108"
  }
  edge-ipr-institution-decision-claims-confirmed "PTAB denies institution (Fintiv / 325(d) / merits)" -> claims-confirmed p 0.35 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 314(a); 37 CFR 42.108"
    note "Denial ends the challenge; claims stand. Institution modeled 0.65 / denial 0.35 (APPROXIMATE, flagged on the node)."
  }
}

decision ipr-trial-instituted: "IPR Trial Instituted" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 316; 37 CFR 42.120–42.121"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Trial instituted. Patent owner options: file the Patent Owner Response, move to amend (substitute claims, intervening rights under 318(c)), or settle before the final written decision to avoid 315(e) estoppel (35 U.S.C. 317)."
  ipr-por-filed "File Patent Owner Response" -> ipr-final-written-decision {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 316; 37 CFR 42.120"
    effort 90.hours
  }
  ipr-mta-filed "File Motion to Amend (substitute claims, 35 U.S.C. 316(d))" -> ipr-final-written-decision {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 316(d); 37 CFR 42.121"
    effort 80.hours
  }
  edge-ipr-trial-instituted-claims-confirmed "Settle before final written decision (35 U.S.C. 317) — avoid estoppel" -> claims-confirmed {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 317; 37 CFR 42.72–42.74"
    effort 20.hours
    valence good
    note "Pre-FWD settlement terminates as to the petitioner and avoids 315(e) estoppel; the Board may terminate rather than proceed. Claims stand."
  }
}

chance ipr-final-written-decision: "IPR Final Written Decision" by office discretion effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 318(a); 37 CFR 42.73"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "The Board's final written decision on the instituted claims. Distribution authored at 0.65 all-cancelled / 0.20 all-upheld / 0.15 mixed-with-substitute — APPROXIMATE; of instituted IPRs reaching a FWD, a majority historically find all instituted claims unpatentable. Estoppel (315(e)) attaches here."
  edge-ipr-final-written-decision-claims-cancelled "FWD: all instituted claims held unpatentable" -> claims-cancelled p 0.65 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 318(a); 318(b)"
  }
  edge-ipr-final-written-decision-claims-confirmed "FWD: claims upheld (patentability confirmed)" -> claims-confirmed p 0.2 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 318(a); 318(b)"
  }
  edge-ipr-final-written-decision-claims-amended "FWD: mixed — substitute claims entered (intervening rights)" -> claims-amended p 0.15 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 318(a); 318(c)"
  }
}

state pgr-petition-filed: "PGR Petition Filed" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 321–324; 37 CFR 42.207"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Petitioner filed a PGR within the 9-month window on broad grounds (incl. 101/112). Patent owner may file a POPR or waive, then the Board rules on institution under the more-likely-than-not standard (35 U.S.C. 324(a))."
  pgr-popr-filed "File Patent Owner Preliminary Response (POPR)" -> pgr-institution-decision {
    authority cite "37 CFR 42.207; 35 U.S.C. 323"
    effort 60.hours
    within pgr-preliminary-response {
      extendable false
      note "POPR due within 3 months of the filing-date notice."
    }
    duration { min 13.5.days, mode 45.days, max 90.days }
  }
  pgr-popr-waived "Waive POPR — reserve arguments for trial" -> pgr-institution-decision {
    authority cite "37 CFR 42.207(b)"
    effort 0.5.hours
  }
}

chance pgr-institution-decision: "PGR Institution Decision" by office discretion effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 324(a); 37 CFR 42.208"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Institution on a showing that it is more likely than not at least one claim is unpatentable. Authored at 0.55 — APPROXIMATE (PGR volume is thin; treated as broadly comparable to IPR institution); flagged."
  edge-pgr-institution-decision-pgr-trial-instituted "PTAB institutes PGR (35 U.S.C. 324(a))" -> pgr-trial-instituted p 0.55 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 324(a); 37 CFR 42.208"
  }
  edge-pgr-institution-decision-claims-confirmed "PTAB denies institution" -> claims-confirmed p 0.45 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 324(a); 37 CFR 42.208"
  }
}

decision pgr-trial-instituted: "PGR Trial Instituted" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 326; 37 CFR 42.220–42.221"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Trial instituted on the broad PGR grounds. Patent owner may respond, move to amend, or settle (35 U.S.C. 327) before the final written decision to escape 325(e) estoppel."
  pgr-por-filed "File Patent Owner Response" -> pgr-final-written-decision {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 326; 37 CFR 42.220"
    effort 90.hours
  }
  pgr-mta-filed "File Motion to Amend (substitute claims, 35 U.S.C. 326(d))" -> pgr-final-written-decision {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 326(d); 37 CFR 42.221"
    effort 80.hours
  }
  edge-pgr-trial-instituted-claims-confirmed "Settle before final written decision (35 U.S.C. 327) — avoid estoppel" -> claims-confirmed {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 327; 37 CFR 42.72–42.74"
    effort 20.hours
    valence good
  }
}

chance pgr-final-written-decision: "PGR Final Written Decision" by office discretion effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 328(a); 37 CFR 42.73"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Final written decision on the instituted claims. Distribution authored 0.60 cancelled / 0.25 upheld / 0.15 mixed — APPROXIMATE; PGR's broader grounds make cancellation modestly likelier than IPR. 325(e) estoppel attaches here."
  edge-pgr-final-written-decision-claims-cancelled "FWD: claims held unpatentable (incl. 101/112 grounds)" -> claims-cancelled p 0.6 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 328(a); 328(b)"
  }
  edge-pgr-final-written-decision-claims-confirmed "FWD: claims upheld" -> claims-confirmed p 0.25 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 328(a); 328(b)"
  }
  edge-pgr-final-written-decision-claims-amended "FWD: mixed — substitute claims entered (intervening rights)" -> claims-amended p 0.15 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 328(a); 328(c)"
  }
}

chance epr-requested: "Ex Parte Reexam Requested" by office discretion effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 302–303; 37 CFR 1.510; MPEP 2209–2214"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "A reexam request is filed (by anyone, even anonymously or the owner). The Office decides within 3 months whether it raises a substantial new question of patentability (SNQ, 35 U.S.C. 303(a)). Grant rate authored at 0.92 — APPROXIMATE; SNQ grants historically run high (~90%+); flagged."
  court_listener_url "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/209660/in-re-swanson/"
  edge-epr-requested-epr-ordered "Director grants reexam — SNQ found (35 U.S.C. 303)" -> epr-ordered p 0.92 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 303(a); 304; 37 CFR 1.515"
  }
  edge-epr-requested-claims-confirmed "Request denied — no substantial new question" -> claims-confirmed p 0.08 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 303(a); 37 CFR 1.515(a)"
    note "Denial (no SNQ) leaves the claims untouched. Grant modeled 0.92 / denial 0.08 (APPROXIMATE, flagged on the node)."
  }
}

decision epr-ordered: "Reexam Ordered" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 304; 37 CFR 1.530(b); MPEP 2249"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Reexamination ordered. The order sets a period of not less than two months for the patent owner's OPTIONAL statement. THE TRAP: filing the statement entitles the third-party requester to a reply (35 U.S.C. 304; 37 CFR 1.535) — usually the owner should decline and wait for the first Office action."
  epr-owner-statement-filed "File Patent Owner Statement (35 U.S.C. 304) — opens requester reply [TRAP]" -> epr-examination {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 304; 37 CFR 1.530(b); MPEP 2249"
    effort 40.hours
    within reexam-owner-statement {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "37 CFR 1.550(c)"
      note "Optional statement due within a period of not less than two months from the order. Filing it entitles the third-party requester to a reply (37 CFR 1.535) — usually a strategic mistake."
    }
    duration { min 9.days, mode 30.days, max 60.days }
    valence bad
  }
  epr-owner-statement-declined "Decline owner statement — reserve for first Office action (recommended)" -> epr-examination {
    authority cite "37 CFR 1.530(b); MPEP 2249"
    effort 0.5.hours
    valence good
  }
}

chance epr-examination: "Reexam Examination → Certificate" by office discretion effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 305–307; 37 CFR 1.550; MPEP 2254"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Ex parte examination proceeds with special dispatch and concludes in a reexamination certificate (35 U.S.C. 307). Distribution authored 0.66 amended/narrowed / 0.22 confirmed / 0.12 all-cancelled — APPROXIMATE; most reexam certificates change or narrow at least some claims. New/amended claims carry intervening rights (35 U.S.C. 307(b))."
  edge-epr-examination-claims-amended "Reexam certificate: claims amended / narrowed" -> claims-amended p 0.66 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 307; 307(b); 37 CFR 1.570"
  }
  edge-epr-examination-claims-confirmed "Reexam certificate: claims confirmed as patentable" -> claims-confirmed p 0.22 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 307; 37 CFR 1.570"
  }
  edge-epr-examination-claims-cancelled "Reexam certificate: claims cancelled" -> claims-cancelled p 0.12 {
    authority cite "35 U.S.C. 307; 37 CFR 1.570"
  }
}

terminal claims-confirmed: "Claims Confirmed (Patent Survives)" outcome [win, confirmed] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 318(b) / 328(b) / 307"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "The challenge failed (denied institution, upheld on the merits, or settled before a final written decision): the claims stand as granted. The patent asset is preserved at (roughly) its issued value. Best terminal in this region for the owner. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $1,000,000, override per matter. Per this terminal's own note, the patent asset is preserved at roughly its issued value."
  valence good
  payoff 1_000_000.usd
}

terminal claims-amended: "Claims Amended / Narrowed" outcome [mixed, amended] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 318(c) / 307(b)"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "Substitute or amended claims survive (via a motion to amend or a reexam certificate). The patent lives on but narrower, and amended claims are subject to INTERVENING RIGHTS (35 U.S.C. 318(c) for AIA trials; 307(b) for reexam) — pre-amendment infringers may be shielded. A partial, discounted win. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $400,000, override per matter, matching this project's partial/mixed-result tier -- per this terminal's own note, 'a partial, discounted win.'"
  valence caution
  payoff 400_000.usd
}

terminal claims-cancelled: "Claims Cancelled (Patent Lost)" outcome [loss, cancelled] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite "35 U.S.C. 318(b) / 328(b) / 307"
{
  group post-grant-group
  note "A final written decision or reexam certificate CANCELS the challenged claims — the patent's asserted claims are gone, the asset largely destroyed after the litigation spend. The worst terminal in this region; the adversarial mirror image of issuance. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $0, override per matter."
  valence bad
  court_listener_url "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4492196/oil-states-energy-services-llc-v-greenes-energy-group-llc/"
  payoff 0.usd
}
